{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "milestone": "M2.19H — BanzAI Engine Hardening, Block 5/5A",
  "description": "The CLOSED registered critical BANZA semantic surface BanzAI must resolve without a model. Assurance material for BanzAI — NOT normative protocol material: every fact here is established elsewhere (the Normative Manifest and the artifacts it indexes, the ADRs, the canonical Reference) and this file only records which questions must reach that truth deterministically, in both languages.",
  "policy": {
    "deterministic_critical": "A stable BANZA architecture fact. Must be SETTLED by the engine with NO model call — a model outage must not remove the answer. Degrading to insufficient, or to a safety refusal, is a FAILURE: refusing to state a published fact is not safety.",
    "supported_synthesis": "Genuinely open-ended: the evidence must be established first, and prose composed from it. Model-backed BY DESIGN. Asserted on evidence and policy, never on wording.",
    "negative_control": "Not a BANZA fact. Must fail closed. Two outcomes are correct and each case declares which: `insufficient` (nothing supports it) or `refused_safe` (the premise is wrong and the engine says so). A confident definition is the failure — and the reason this class exists is that closing coverage must never be able to buy an invented answer.",
    "acceptance": "100% EXPECTED SEMANTIC OUTCOME — not 100% deterministic answers. A correct refusal for a negative control PASSES. An invented definition for an unregistered profile FAILS. The aggregate percentage is not the target and must never be optimised on its own.",
    "pairing": "`pair` links the PT and EN forms of ONE question. Paired cases must reach the same record and the same policy: one canonical fact, localized surfaces — never two independently editable truths.",
    "prose": "Answer strings are NOT asserted. Localized prose may evolve; the subject, the policy, the establishing evidence and the prohibited relations may not."
  },
